{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1793530828","published":"2026-11-01T11:01:17Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:16:25.326768521Z","upstream":["CVE-2021-4037","CVE-2026-53176","CVE-2026-90103","CVE-2026-90203","CVE-2026-90223","CVE-2026-90225","CVE-2026-90382","CVE-2026-90413","CVE-2026-90435","CVE-2026-92498","CVE-2026-93054","CVE-2026-93104","CVE-2026-93262","CVE-2026-93803","CVE-2026-93820","CVE-2026-97408","CVE-2026-97427","CVE-2026-97448","CVE-2026-97509","CVE-2026-97539","CVE-2026-97564","CVE-2026-97596","CVE-2026-97908","CVE-2026-97940","CVE-2026-98077","CVE-2026-98096","CVE-2026-98348","CVE-2026-98357","CVE-2026-98432"],"summary":"Fix of 30 CVEs","details":"   * Bump kernel ABI to 32: ship the ELS kernel as 4.19.0-32-*, distinct from\n     the prior 4.19.0-31.\n   * CVE-2021-4037\n     - xfs: fix up non-directory creation in SGID directories\n       {CVE-2021-4037}\n     - fs: add mode_strip_sgid() helper {CVE-2021-4037}\n     - fs: move S_ISGID stripping into the vfs_*() helpers\n       {CVE-2021-4037}\n   * CVE-2026-53176\n     - IB/isert: Reject login PDUs shorter than ISER_HEADERS_LEN\n       {CVE-2026-53176}\n   * CVE-2026-90103\n     - NFSv4.2: fix LAYOUTSTATS send buffer exhaustion {CVE-2026-90103}\n   * CVE-2026-90203\n     - Squashfs: check block offset is not negative {CVE-2026-90203}\n   * CVE-2026-90223\n     - nfc: llcp: bound SNL TLV parsing to the skb and add length checks\n       {CVE-2026-90223}\n   * CVE-2026-90225\n     - nfc: llcp: read llcp_sock->local under the socket lock in\n       getsockopt {CVE-2026-90225}\n   * CVE-2026-90382\n     - wifi: mt76: mt76x02: do not WARN on invalid rx descriptor length\n       {CVE-2026-90382}\n   * CVE-2026-90413\n     - IB/isert: reject login PDUs declaring more data than was received\n       {CVE-2026-90413}\n   * CVE-2026-90435\n     - RDMA/mlx5: Fix integer overflow of user QP buffer size\n       {CVE-2026-90435}\n   * CVE-2026-92498\n     - wifi: ath6kl: avoid buffer overreads in WMI event handlers\n       {CVE-2026-92498}\n   * CVE-2026-93054\n     - uio: Fix stale info pointer in failed registration path\n       {CVE-2026-93054}\n   * CVE-2026-93104\n     - RDMA/rvt: Return NULL after port allocation failure\n       {CVE-2026-93104}\n   * CVE-2026-93262\n     - md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush()\n       {CVE-2026-93262}\n   * CVE-2026-93803\n     - wifi: libipw: fix key index receive bound checks {CVE-2026-93803}\n   * CVE-2026-93820\n     - PCI: rockchip: Protect root bus removal with rescan lock\n       {CVE-2026-93820}\n   * CVE-2026-97408\n     - Bluetooth: L2CAP: validate connectionless PSM length\n       {CVE-2026-97408}\n   * CVE-2026-97427\n     - drm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy {CVE-2026-97427}\n   * CVE-2026-97448\n     - ACPICA: Add validation for node in acpi_ns_build_normalized_path()\n       {CVE-2026-97448}\n   * CVE-2026-97509\n     - thunderbolt: Keep XDomain reference during the lifetime of a\n       service {CVE-2026-97509}\n   * CVE-2026-97539\n     - usb: xusbatm: don't rely on id table pointer arithmetic\n       {CVE-2026-97539}\n   * CVE-2026-97564\n     - smb: client: reject userspace cifs.idmap descriptions\n       {CVE-2026-97564}\n   * CVE-2026-97596\n     - ipvs: reject invalid states in connection template sync records\n       {CVE-2026-97596}\n   * CVE-2026-97908\n     - Bluetooth: btqcomsmd: destroy RPMsg endpoints before freeing\n       hci_dev {CVE-2026-97908}\n   * CVE-2026-97940\n     - ipv6: fix fib6 walker UAF on seq stop {CVE-2026-97940}\n   * CVE-2026-98077\n     - netfilter: nf_conntrack_sip: fix OOB read in sip_skip_whitespace()\n       {CVE-2026-98077}\n   * CVE-2026-98096\n     - ipv6: sr: restore network header before routing and forwarding\n       {CVE-2026-98096}\n   * CVE-2026-98348\n     - wifi: libipw: reject too-short association responses\n       {CVE-2026-98348}\n   * CVE-2026-98357\n     - IB/isert: wait for deferred control PDU completions before\n       releasing the connection {CVE-2026-98357}\n   * CVE-2026-98432\n     - ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period\n       {CVE-2026-98432}\n   * Miscellaneous upstream changes\n     - sunrpc: clear XPRT_SOCK_UPD_TIMEOUT when reset transport","affected":[{"package":{"name":"hyperv-daemons","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/hyperv-daemons?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-5+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1793530828.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libbpf-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libbpf-dev?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-5+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1793530828.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libbpf4.19","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libbpf4.19?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-5+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1793530828.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libcpupower-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libcpupower-dev?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-5+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1793530828.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libcpupower1","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libcpupower1?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-5+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debi